# IC-7760 CI-V command catalog extracted from IC-7760 CI-V reference guide (A7788-8EX-2, May 2025). Format CMD|SUB|DATA|NAME|NOTES
# Default address B2h (RF deck/controller), controller E0h. Frame FE FE <to> <from> Cn [Sc] [data] FD ; OK=FB, NG=FA. Baud rate setting only needed when connected to the [REMOTE] jack of the RF deck (USB B port of the controller: no baud setting).
# Asterisk (*) = send/read data. '29' in NOTES (written as [29]) = the command is marked '29' in the manual's Sub cmd column = supported by the Main/Sub direct-specify command 29 (frame: FE FE B2 E0 29 <00=MAIN|01=SUB> <cmd> [sub] [data] FD; manual: when OK(FB)/NG(FA) is received the '29' and the Main/Sub byte are omitted; for data replies the manual does not say - UNSURE).
# Footnotes: *1 1A 05 01 63, 1A 08, 1A 0A, 1A 0D cannot be sent (read only); *2 ANT RX-I/O type: 01 invalid, 00 always returned; *3 ANT-RX I/O 01 invalid if type is RX-ANT; *4 CW msg sent in CW mode when transmitting or break-in ON; *5 18 01 power ON works via [USB B] port of controller when in Standby/Shutdown, not via [REMOTE] jack; *6 27 11 valid only with [REMOTE] jack or [USB B] port connected.
# FREQ = BCD 5 bytes LSB first: [10Hz 1Hz][1kHz 100Hz][100kHz 10kHz][10MHz 1MHz][1GHz 100MHz]
00||FREQ BCD 5 bytes (see p.17)|Send the frequency data (transceive)|
01||MODE bytes (see p.17)|Send the mode data (transceive)|
02||BAND EDGE (see p.17)|Read the band edge frequencies|
03||FREQ BCD 5 bytes|Read the operating frequency|
04||MODE 2 bytes mode,filter|Read the operating mode|
05||FREQ BCD 5 bytes|Set the operating frequency|
06||MODE bytes mode[,filter]|Set the operating mode|mode 00 LSB,01 USB,02 AM,03 CW,04 RTTY,05 FM,07 CW-R,08 RTTY-R,12 PSK,13 PSK-R; filter 01 FIL1,02 FIL2,03 FIL3 (may be skipped)
07||(none)|Select the VFO mode|[29]
07|B0||Exchange Main and Sub bands|
07|B1||Equalize Main and Sub bands|
07|C0||Turn OFF Dualwatch|
07|C1||Turn ON Dualwatch|
07|C2|00/01|Send/read the Dualwatch setting|send/read (*); 00=OFF 01=ON
07|D0||Select the Main band|
07|D1||Select the Sub band|
07|D2|00 or 01|Send/read Main/Sub band selection|send/read (*); 00=Main band selection 01=Sub band selection
08||(none)|Select the Memory mode|
08||BCD 2 bytes 00 01 ~ 00 99|Select the Memory channel|00 01=M-CH01 00 99=M-CH99
08||BCD 2 bytes 01 00|Select program scan edge channel P1|
08||BCD 2 bytes 01 01|Select program scan edge channel P2|
09||(none)|Memory write|
0A||(none)|Memory copy to VFO|
0B||(none)|Memory clear|
0E|00||Cancel the scan|
0E|01||Start a Programmed/memory scan|
0E|02||Start a Programmed scan|
0E|03||Start a F scan|
0E|12||Start a Fine programmed scan|
0E|13||Start a Fine F scan|
0E|22||Start a Memory scan|
0E|23||Start a Select memory scan|
0E|A1~A7||Select F scan span|x=1~7: +-5,+-10,+-20,+-50,+-100,+-500 kHz,+-1 MHz
0E|B0||Clear the Select channel setting|
0E|B1||Set as select channel|previously set number by CI-V after power ON, or 1 if none selected
0E|B1|01 ~ 03|Set the channel as a Select channel|01=SEL1 02=SEL2 03=SEL3
0E|B2|00 ~ 03|Set the Select memory scan channel|00=ALL 01=SEL1 02=SEL2 03=SEL3
0E|D0||Set Scan resume OFF|
0E|D3||Set Scan resume ON (Close&Delay)|
0F||(none) request, reply 00/01|Read Split setting|00=Split OFF 01=Split ON
0F|00||Set Split function OFF|
0F|01||Set Split function ON|
10||00 ~ 08|Send/read the tuning step|send/read (*); 00=OFF (10Hz or 1Hz),01=100Hz,02=1kHz,03=5kHz,04=9kHz,05=10kHz,06=12.5kHz,07=20kHz,08=25kHz
11||BCD 1 byte 00,03,06,09,12,15,18,21,24,27,30,33,36,39,42,45|Send/read attenuator|send/read (*); [29]; value = dB, 00=OFF
12|00|00/01|Select/read ANT1 selection|send/read (*); [29]; 00=RX ANT OFF 01=RX ANT ON; footnote *2
12|01|00/01|Select/read ANT2 selection|send/read (*); [29]; footnote *2
12|02|00/01|Select/read ANT3 selection|send/read (*); [29]; footnote *2
12|03|00/01|Select/read ANT4 selection|send/read (*); [29]; footnote *2
13|00||Speak all data by the voice synthesizer|S meter level, frequency and mode
13|01||Speak the operating frequency and S meter level|
13|02||Speak the operating mode|announced after ongoing speech
14|01|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read the AF level|send/read (*); [29]; 00 00=min 02 55=max
14|02|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read the RF gain level|[29]; 00 00=min 02 55=max
14|03|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read the squelch level|[29]; 00 00=min 02 55=max
14|05|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read the APF position|[29]; 10 Hz steps; 00 00=Pitch-550 Hz 01 28=Pitch 02 55=Pitch+550 Hz
14|06|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read the NR level|[29]; 00 00=0% 02 55=100%
14|07|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read TWIN PBT (PBT1) position|[29]; 00 00=max CCW 01 28=center 02 55=max CW
14|08|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read TWIN PBT (PBT2) position|[29]; 00 00=max CCW 01 28=center 02 55=max CW
14|09|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read CW pitch|5 Hz steps; 00 00=300 Hz 01 28=600 Hz 02 55=900 Hz (no [29] mark)
14|0A|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read the selected band's RF power|00 00=min 02 55=max
14|0B|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read MIC gain|00 00=min 02 55=max
14|0C|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read keying speed|00 00=6 WPM 02 55=48 WPM
14|0D|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read Notch filter setting|[29]; 00 00=max CCW 01 28=center 02 55=max CW
14|0E|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read the COMP level|00 00=0 02 55=10
14|0F|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read the Break-IN delay|00 00=2.0d 02 55=13.0d
14|12|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read NB level|[29]; 00 00=0% 02 55=100%
14|13|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read the DIGI-SEL shift amount|[29]; 00 00=min 02 55=max
14|14|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read DRIVE Gain|00 00=0% 02 55=100%
14|15|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read Monitor audio [MONI] level|00 00=0% 02 55=100%
14|16|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read the VOX gain|00 00=0% 02 55=100%
14|17|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read the Anti VOX gain|00 00=0% 02 55=100%
14|19|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Send/read LCD backlight brightness|00 00=0% 02 55=100%
15|01|00/01|Read noise or S-meter squelch status|[29]; 00=Close 01=Open
15|02|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Read S-meter level|[29]; 00 00=S0 01 20=S9 02 41=S9+60 dB
15|05|00/01|Read various squelch (tone squelch etc) status|[29]; 00=Close 01=Open
15|07|00/01|Read the OVF status|[29]; 00=OVF indicator OFF 01=ON
15|11|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Read the Po meter level|00 00=0W 01 43=100W 02 12=200W
15|12|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Read SWR meter level|00 00=SWR1.0 00 48=1.5 00 80=2.0 01 20=3.0
15|13|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Read ALC meter level|00 00=min 01 20=max
15|14|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Read COMP meter level|00 00=0 dB 01 30=15 dB 02 41=30 dB
15|15|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Read Vd meter level|00 00=0 V 01 51=44 V 02 11=52 V
15|16|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Read Id meter level|00 00=0 A 00 77=5 A 01 65=10 A 02 41=15 A
16|02|00,01,02|Preamp|send/read (*); [29]; 00=Preamp OFF 01=Preamp 1 ON 02=Preamp 2 ON
16|12|01 ~ 03|Send/read the AGC time constant|[29]; 01=FAST 02=MID 03=SLOW
16|22|00/01|Send/read the Noise blanker|[29]; 00=OFF 01=ON
16|32|00,01,02,03|Audio peak filter|[29]; 00=OFF 01=WIDE ON (320 Hz if SHARP APF) 02=MID ON (160 Hz) 03=NAR ON (80 Hz)
16|40|00/01|Send/read the Noise reduction|[29]; 00=OFF 01=ON
16|41|00/01|Send/read the Auto Notch function|[29]; 00=OFF 01=ON
16|42|00/01|Send/read the Repeater tone|[29]; 00=OFF 01=ON
16|43|00/01|Send/read the Tone squelch|[29]; 00=OFF 01=ON
16|44|00/01|Send/read the Speech compressor|00=OFF 01=ON
16|45|00/01|Send/read the Monitor [MONI] function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|46|00/01|Send/read the VOX function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|47|00,01,02|BK-IN function|00=OFF 01=Semi BK-IN ON 02=Full BK-IN ON
16|48|00/01|Send/read the Manual Notch function|[29]; 00=OFF 01=ON
16|4E|00/01|Send/read the DIGI-SEL function|[29]; 00=OFF 01=ON
16|4F|00/01|Send/read the Twin peak filter|[29]; 00=OFF 01=ON; ON only when Mark=2125 Hz and Shift=170 Hz
16|50|00/01|Send/read the Dial Lock function|00=OFF 01=ON; main dial or panel locked depending on Lock Function (1A 05 00 77)
16|53|00/01|Send/read the ANT-RX I/O|[29]; 00=OFF 01=ON; footnote *3
16|56|00/01|Send/read DSP IF filter type|[29]; 00=SHARP 01=SOFT
16|57|00 ~ 02|Send/read the Manual Notch width|[29]; 00=WIDE 01=MID 02=NAR
16|58|00 ~ 02|Send/read SSB transmit bandwidth|00=WIDE 01=MID 02=NAR; applied value depends on COMP: WIDE=1A 05 00 15, MID=1A 05 00 16, NAR=1A 05 00 17
16|5E|00/01|MAIN/SUB Tracking function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|65|00/01|Set the IP Plus function|[29]; 00=OFF 01=ON
16|66|00/01|Send/read the TX Inhibit function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|67|00/01|Send/read the DPD function|00=OFF 01=ON
17||ASCII text up to 30 chars (see p.17)|Send CW messages|footnote *4; FF stops sending; ^ = no inter-character space
18|00||Turn OFF the transceiver|
18|01||Turn ON the transceiver|footnote *5
19|00||Read the transceiver ID|
1A|00|see p.19|Send/read memory contents|send/read (*)
1A|01|see p.18|Send/read band stacking register contents|
1A|02|see p.20|Send/read memory keyer contents|
1A|03|see p.20|Send/read the selected IF filter width|[29]
1A|04|see p.20|Send/read the selected AGC time constant|[29]
1A|05 00 01|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] RX > SSB > Send/read RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 02|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] RX > SSB > Send/read RX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 03|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] RX > SSB > Send/read RX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 04|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] RX > AM > Send/read RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 05|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] RX > AM > Send/read RX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 06|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] RX > AM > Send/read RX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 07|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] RX > FM > Send/read RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 08|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] RX > FM > Send/read RX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 09|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] RX > FM > Send/read RX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 10|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] RX > CW > Send/read RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 11|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] RX > RTTY > Send/read RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 12|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] RX > PSK > Send/read RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 13|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] TX > SSB > Send/read TX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 14|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] TX > SSB > Send/read TX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 15|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] TX > SSB > Send/read TX bandwidth for wide|
1A|05 00 16|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] TX > SSB > Send/read TX bandwidth for mid|
1A|05 00 17|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] TX > SSB > Send/read TX bandwidth for narrow|
1A|05 00 18|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] TX > SSB-D > Send/read TX bandwidth|
1A|05 00 19|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] TX > AM > Send/read TX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 20|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] TX > AM > Send/read TX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 21|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] TX > FM > Send/read TX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 22|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW] TX > FM > Send/read TX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 23|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|[SET > Function] Send/read the Beep Level setting|(00 00=Minimum ~ 02 55=Maximum)
1A|05 00 24|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Send/read the Beep Level Limit setting|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 25|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Send/read the Beep (Confirmation) setting|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 26|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 03|[SET > Function] Send/read the Band Edge Beep setting|( 00=OFF, 01=ON (Default), 02=ON (User), 03=ON (User) & TX Limit)
1A|05 00 27|BCD 2 bytes 00 50 ~ 02 00|[SET > Function] Function > Beep Sound (MAIN)|(00 50=500 Hz ~ 02 00=2000 Hz)
1A|05 00 28|BCD 2 bytes 00 50 ~ 02 00|[SET > Function] Function > Beep Sound (SUB)|(00 50=500 Hz ~ 02 00=2000 Hz)
1A|05 00 29|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Send/read the Speaker MAIN/SUB Mix|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 30|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|[SET > Function] RF/SQL Control|(00=Auto, 01=SQL, 02=RF+SQL)
1A|05 00 31|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Send/read the Cancel CI-V Remote Set Levels|( 00=All Volume Levels, 01=Operated Volume Level)
